Phase 2 — Subject and Birth-Time Foundation

Objective

Implement the subject model, birth data, confidence states, and rectification workflow.

Deliverables

• Subject creation and update service.
• Birth date and location validation.
• Birth-time states:
  • EXACT
  • RECTIFIED
  • UNKNOWN
• Rectification session model.
• Rectification round model.
• Candidate time-window model.
• Recognition summary model.
• Selected-window and estimated-time model.
• Birth-time confidence calculation.

Rectification workflow

1. Generate candidate birth-time windows.
2. Calculate native signals for each candidate.
3. Generate recognition summaries.
4. Collect user recognition or rejection.
5. Narrow the candidate window.
6. Repeat until:
  • a selected estimate is reached;
  • the confidence threshold is met;
  • or the result remains unresolved.

Dependencies

• Phase 1 schemas.
• At least one native calculation engine from Phase 3.

Acceptance criteria

• Exact birth times remain distinct from rectified times.
• Rectification sessions preserve every candidate window and recognition response.
• The system can represent multiple rounds of narrowing.
• A selected estimated birth time includes its confidence and supporting evidence.
• If no candidate is sufficiently supported, the result remains unresolved.
• Rectification does not overwrite the original reported birth-time data.
• Every downstream calculation identifies whether it used exact, rectified, or unknown birth time.

