Alignment rules

The engine must distinguish:

1. Objective condition present and subjectively reported.
2. Objective condition present but not subjectively reported.
3. Objective condition absent or unsupported but subjectively reported.
4. Both objective and subjective layers unknown.
5. Objective and subjective layers aligned.
6. Objective and subjective layers mismatched.
7. Objective data disputed or historically uncertain.

Dependencies

• Phase 4 objective environment.
• Phase 5 subjective exposure.
• Phase 1 schemas.

Acceptance criteria

• The same objective environment can be associated with different subjective exposure records for different people.
• A mismatch is preserved rather than resolved automatically.
• A benign objective environment cannot invalidate a reported experience.
• An objectively adverse environment cannot create a subjective experience record without user or evidence support.
• Incubator recognition remains separate from portal recognition.
• The incubator can be evaluated even when one layer is unknown.
• The system can explain why an incubator is aligned, mismatched, partial, or unresolved.

