3.4 Privacy and Sensitive Data

Subjective exposure may contain sensitive information about violence, neglect, poverty, family conflict, control, religion, politics, and bodily stress.

Required controls:

• explicit consent;
• field-level access control;
• encryption at rest and in transit;
• audit logging;
• deletion and export workflows;
• redaction support;
• separation of personally identifying data from interpretive records where feasible.

Acceptance criteria

A user can view, export, correct, restrict, and delete subjective exposure records according to policy.

